  "label": "Man running away from pregnancy news",
  "description": "The text 'i just heard my girlfriend is pregnant' is mapped onto the visual of the man running away, implying that the man represents the speaker ('i') who is reacting to the news by running away. This is a classic analogical mapping in memes where the visual subject is identified as the textual subject ('me').",
